.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH snip-man 1  "snip 0.3.1" 
.SH NAME
snip\-man \- Install, inspect, or export the embedded manual pages
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsnip man\fR [\fB\-\-library\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Install, inspect, or export the embedded manual pages
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-library\fR \fI<LIBRARY>\fR
Library root. Falls back to SNIP_LIBRARY, ancestor discovery, then config
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR
Structured output mode for commands that return records
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
jsonl
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR
Color policy for terminal preview
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
snip\-man\-path(1)
Print the resolved man page installation directory
.TP
snip\-man\-install(1)
Install all manual pages
.TP
snip\-man\-uninstall(1)
Remove unmodified pages recorded by snip
.TP
snip\-man\-show(1)
Show an embedded manual page with the system man viewer
.TP
snip\-man\-generate(1)
Export all embedded manual pages to a directory
